19
00:02:03,713 --> 00:02:08,519
For six of those 12 finalists, the Olympic Games is a new experience.

20
00:02:08,538 --> 00:02:14,186
Unlike for Steve Rebiliad sitting next to me, Steve, you've been studying the scores over the two rounds so far.

21
00:02:14,626 --> 00:02:18,730
I mean, how much has the standard just built as this competition has progressed?

22
00:02:19,031 --> 00:02:24,197
I think it's really significant, Roger, that from the men in the top 12 who've qualified for this final,

23
00:02:24,176 --> 00:02:33,409
The lowest dive score in the semi was 72 and that from Riley McCormick and even that scored eights but with a low tariff so the consistency's really been building.

24
00:02:33,509 --> 00:02:37,415
In the preliminaries we saw dives in the 30s and even a couple in the 20s.

25
00:02:37,795 --> 00:02:53,138
The lift in consistency for the second phase of the competition was remarkable and now what we're looking for is consistency with high quality and that's what we're seeing from Chu and Lin and it's hard to see them being displaced from the top two positions

26
00:02:53,117 --> 00:03:01,497
