01:27:13,666 --> 01:27:15,228
This was beautiful.

888
01:27:16,009 --> 01:27:16,609
Tight tuck.

889
01:27:16,930 --> 01:27:17,851
Look at the finish here.

890
01:27:18,311 --> 01:27:20,595
Absolutely vertical by the time he hits the water.

891
01:27:20,635 --> 01:27:22,237
The splash is barely there.

892
01:27:23,118 --> 01:27:24,539
And he is richly rewarded.

893
01:27:25,641 --> 01:27:30,268
But hold on, folks, because there's some tough dives with bigger difficulty coming.

894
01:27:30,484 --> 01:27:35,010
He knows though that he has put on the big show and he will be delighted at that.

895
01:27:40,154 --> 01:27:47,101
And the young lad comes through for the first time rather than the more introverted figure in competition.

896
01:27:47,221 --> 01:27:51,105
Now, David Budaya has responded to every challenge.

897
01:27:52,608 --> 01:27:54,630
A mature American diver now.

898
01:27:55,211 --> 01:27:57,493
This he will believe is his moment.

899
01:27:57,512 --> 01:27:59,074
Three point six his tariff.

900
01:27:59,095 --> 01:28:00,095
We've got to emphasize that.

901
01:28:00,377 --> 01:28:04,220
Back two and a half somersault, two and a half twist.

902
01:28:05,045 --> 01:28:06,046
Oh, it's good too.

903
01:28:07,046 --> 01:28:09,670
And Tom Daly's got to be concerned about that.

904
01:28:09,710 --> 01:28:14,854
It only needs to beat him by one point and he's out of the gold medal position.

905
01:28:17,077 --> 01:28:19,720
And Budaya waits and hopes.

906
01:28:20,720 --> 01:28:22,322
What a competition he's put together.

907
01:28:22,341 --> 01:28:26,105
24 hours ago, he was nearly out of it.

908
01:28:27,367 --> 01:28:28,108
He's relaxed.

909
01:28:28,148 --> 01:28:30,029
He said he relaxed and he's been enjoying it.

910
01:28:31,131 --> 01:28:33,132
And this is nail biting.

911
01:28:33,673 --> 01:28:34,173
Oh!

912
01:28:35,858 --> 01:28:36,539
He's there.

913
01:28:36,560 --> 01:28:38,404
Oh, he's more than there, 102.6.

914
01:28:40,511 --> 01:28:42,877
He has stormed to top position.

915
01:28:46,707 --> 01:28:50,137
Oh, what a moment for this man, a career highlight.

916
01:28:52,362 --> 01:28:54,786
But it's not over yet.

917
01:28:55,086 --> 01:29:00,573
It's still the favorite to go, not to mention Lin Yue.

918
01:29:00,634 --> 01:29:06,422
Only one diver in the last three games from China has missed out on a 10 meter medal.

919
01:29:07,564 --> 01:29:12,953
So he will be feeling in this rare opportunity to compete individually that he has missed the boat.

920
01:29:15,059 --> 01:29:18,182
Back two and a half somersault, two and a half twists.

921
01:29:18,203 --> 01:29:19,305
It's not good enough.

922
01:29:19,404 --> 01:29:21,828
There was a separation of the ankles.

923
01:29:21,929 --> 01:29:24,351
The entry wasn't quite right.

924
01:29:25,052 --> 01:29:27,256
And it's not quite good enough, I would feel.

925
01:29:28,177 --> 01:29:29,279
And I'd leave it to the judges.

926
01:29:29,359 --> 01:29:34,707
But uncharacteristically, the ankles not locked together.

927
01:29:35,507 --> 01:29:38,192
The splash, too big.

928
01:29:39,193 --> 01:29:40,515
The chance for medals.

929
01:29:42,939 --> 01:29:43,800
They're not used to it.

930
01:29:43,819 --> 01:29:44,661
Chen Raolin.

931
01:29:46,564 --> 01:29:50,011
The women's champion we saw down there on the bench.

932
01:29:50,030 --> 01:29:51,353
They're all out there supporting.

933
01:29:51,393 --> 01:29:55,259
They came here for the clean sweep of eight golds.

934
01:29:55,640 --> 01:29:56,600
They're looking for seven.

935
01:29:57,462 --> 01:29:58,725
They may have to settle for six.

936
01:29:59,164 --> 01:30:01,368
Tom Daly knows he's got a medal.

937
01:30:01,429 --> 01:30:02,270
It's just what color.

938
01:30:02,631 --> 01:30:03,591
So does Budaya.

939
01:30:04,713 --> 01:30:06,497
Because there's just one man to come.

940
01:30:08,265 --> 01:30:10,568
You can see the pressure just lifted off Tom Daley.

941
01:30:11,288 --> 01:30:23,601
That re-dive, that opening re-dive, well, Chubo, the pre-race favorite, as it were, back two and a half somersault, two and a half twist, the last dive of these Olympic Games.

942
01:30:24,502 --> 01:30:28,065
What a competition.

943
01:30:28,086 --> 01:30:31,470
Well, it was good, but is it a hundred dive?

944
01:30:32,270 --> 01:30:33,851
Budaya might be the man.

945
01:30:35,636 --> 01:30:41,423
Choubo lost that 2009 World Championships to Tom Daley right in the final dive.

946
01:30:41,965 --> 01:30:42,985
He knows what it's like.

947
01:30:45,048 --> 01:30:47,712
Just not quite perfect with the entry.

948
01:30:47,731 --> 01:30:50,676
There was a bigger splash than we're used to seeing from this man.

949
01:30:52,377 --> 01:30:54,100
Through the air, beautiful.

950
01:30:54,841 --> 01:30:57,984
The finish, not the very best impression he could leave.

951
01:30:58,585 --> 01:31:00,146
He wants to see what this is.

952
01:31:01,970 --> 01:31:04,733
And he's forced his way between Badaer and Daley.

953
01:31:06,974 --> 01:31:08,737
So Budaya is your champion.

954
01:31:09,457 --> 01:31:22,336
David Budaya of America follows in the great tradition, the great days are back for American diving and the Chinese have to settle for second place with Chubo, the favorite.

955
01:31:22,817 --> 01:31:25,761
Tom Daly gets the bronze.

956
01:31:25,780 --> 01:31:34,432
A brilliant, dramatic, staggering competition and David Budaya comes out of the pool on top of the world.

957
01:31:35,712 --> 01:31:42,640
Well, it's a competition that anyone who's seen it here or at home will remember for many a day.

958
01:31:44,442 --> 01:31:52,390
We've had all sorts of drama here, but Chu Bo is crushed by coming up short.

959
01:31:52,911 --> 01:31:57,676
Coming up short to 9.509, and that is not enough.

960
01:31:57,756 --> 01:32:04,503
And Tom Daley knows how tough it is to get a medal in this 10-metre platform diving event.

961
01:32:05,817 --> 01:32:11,537
And he is the first Briton since Brian Phelps back in 1960, 52 years ago.

962
01:32:11,577 --> 01:32:15,168
And David Butaya.

963
01:32:16,465 --> 01:32:20,411
bringing the good times back to diving in the United States.

964
01:32:21,592 --> 01:32:22,895
Sun Bo has to settle.

965
01:32:24,337 --> 01:32:25,238
Steve, your thoughts?

966
01:32:25,600 --> 01:32:29,164
Well, I'm just staggered at Budaya's competition.

967
01:32:29,905 --> 01:32:35,956
You know, last night he was inconsistent, he was all over the place, he fell into the semi-final.

968
01:32:36,237 --> 01:32:42,185
Then he impressed us, Budaya, by qualifying in third best position and now he's won it.

969
01:32:45,322 --> 01:32:51,307
And that top score of 102.6 for his final dive just blew them away.

970
01:32:51,347 --> 01:32:57,073
And Chou Bow, five dives in the 90 and a 100, not good enough.

971
01:32:57,533 --> 01:32:59,036
That tells you how good Bodaya was.

972
01:32:59,115 --> 01:33:02,319
And Tom Daly has thrilled this British crowd.

973
01:33:02,679 --> 01:33:11,228
I just feel privileged to be sitting here to have seen it and to have enjoyed it and to watch these men under pressure perform.

974
01:33:12,018 --> 01:33:23,698
so exciting and you experience this for a massive crowd not used to big crowds in diving events in this country and they have seen something quite unforgettable

975
01:33:24,100 --> 01:33:26,323
and never presume it's over.

976
01:33:26,483 --> 01:33:28,666
Chubo a tearful figure.

977
01:33:28,726 --> 01:33:31,149
He has had his success.

978
01:33:31,650 --> 01:33:41,944
David Boudia, 23 year old from Abilene in Texas will feel that he has worked for this and he's worked for this over three sessions.

979
01:33:42,846 --> 01:33:44,850
It's in there sharing the tears.

980
01:33:46,631 --> 01:33:49,416
They win together and lose

981
01:33:50,542 --> 01:33:54,649
The stars and stripes are getting ready to be unfurled and hang high.

982
01:33:54,990 --> 01:33:57,255
A great respect from all the divers.

983
01:33:57,295 --> 01:34:00,220
They know this has been a great competition.

984
01:34:01,561 --> 01:34:11,538
Well, they were expected to and Lynn to take the top two places, but there's only room for one of them on the podium and it'll be a silver medal.

985
01:34:16,278 --> 01:34:20,145
And Budaya has come from 10th four years ago to first in London.

986
01:34:21,588 --> 01:34:25,216
It's been a long journey and a very successful and happy one for him now.

987
01:34:25,275 --> 01:34:29,625
He's dominated at home in the States, 16 national titles.

988
01:34:31,006 --> 01:34:31,788
He's won.

989
01:34:33,506 --> 01:34:39,735
And the United States, this is their 129th diving medal.

990
01:34:40,095 --> 01:34:45,162
They used to dominate before the Chinese entered the games and then stole their show.

991
01:34:45,564 --> 01:34:49,970
But now this will mean so much to them to be back on top of the platform.

992
01:34:50,690 --> 01:34:55,597
And we know about David that originally with this discipline, he was scared of heights.

993
01:34:55,738 --> 01:34:57,820
He had some work done with the sports psychologist.

994
01:34:57,841 --> 01:35:00,645
He now describes it as a walk in the park.

995
01:35:00,625 --> 01:35:06,697
Well, wherever he walks now, he's going to be recognized as a gold medalist and someone who won a most extraordinary competition here.

996
01:35:07,599 --> 01:35:18,140
And by less than two points from Chubo and Tom Daly, ten behind Chubo, but well clear a victim in a bay of an absolutely worthy medalist.

997
01:35:19,502 --> 01:35:20,083
Oh, my goodness.

998
01:35:20,324 --> 01:35:21,587
What a competition, Roger.

999
01:35:21,635 --> 01:35:23,860
Lin Yue will be distraught.

1000
01:35:24,523 --> 01:35:27,770
Their expectations and the pressure on them is so high.

1001
01:35:28,613 --> 01:35:35,712
And for many of these divers, their time will come again, just teenagers, half the field remember, it was their first Olympic Games.

1002
01:35:38,662 --> 01:35:56,506
And the great Greg Luganis being introduced to the crowd, the real idol of American diving, an iconic figure, and he, more than anyone, will be delighted to see an American right at the top of diving's Blue Ribbon event.

1003
01:35:58,609 --> 01:36:00,332
Such a buzz in this place as well.

1004
01:36:01,154 --> 01:36:05,800
You don't have to know a lot about diving to know you've been at something special.

1005
01:36:06,353 --> 01:36:10,443
Now Louganis a winner of this event in Los Angeles and Seoul.

1006
01:36:14,192 --> 01:36:17,460
Klaus Diabasi of Italy won it three in a row.

1007
01:36:22,164 --> 01:36:24,269
and the British team all in there.

1008
01:36:24,670 --> 01:36:27,213
They know what pressure Tom's been under.

1009
01:36:27,975 --> 01:36:33,345
Of course, his father died and he'd been such a support and a presence to him.

1010
01:36:33,405 --> 01:36:40,899
He'd been bullied at school all his life seems to be played out in a public spotlight but

1011
01:36:40,880 --> 01:36:47,110
And let's go back again to that first dive where he was distracted by camera flashes in the crowd.

1012
01:36:47,431 --> 01:36:50,237
He was given a 75.6 wisely.

1013
01:36:50,596 --> 01:36:51,979
He and his coach appealed.

1014
01:36:52,400 --> 01:36:54,203
Fina took a sympathetic view.

1015
01:36:54,824 --> 01:37:02,078
He redived and went from 75.6 to 91.2 and that proved absolutely crucial.

1016
01:37:03,592 --> 01:37:09,890
It took some nerve to do that, to have the professionalism to say that.

1017
01:37:10,109 --> 01:37:11,755
It's all history now.

1018
01:37:13,399 --> 01:37:19,375
Actually, when you look at the margin between third and fourth, it was more than the 15 points.

1019
01:37:19,354 --> 01:37:25,465
In the end, there won't be any protests from those beneath him because he was so clearly in third place.

1020
01:37:26,426 --> 01:37:35,600
And that's of some comfort, I think, to anyone who might have wanted to question whether he should have been allowed to re-dive because the margin made sure it wasn't an issue in the end.

1021
01:37:35,619 --> 01:37:37,884
But it did have a massive effect on his confidence.

1022
01:37:38,003 --> 01:37:40,547
Absolutely, yeah.

1023
01:37:40,568 --> 01:37:44,434
Put him in contention and ask questions of Baddaya and Choubo.

1024
01:37:46,979 --> 01:37:53,824
And he's getting all the coverage here because of his special place in the British consciousness.

1025
01:37:54,506 --> 01:37:58,168
He and Jessica Ennis were the two poster boy and girl.

1026
01:37:58,770 --> 01:38:03,213
He will feel as though he's got his gold really by being on that podium.

1027
01:38:06,356 --> 01:38:15,905
David Budaya though will take all the plaudits and Chubo with an Olympic silver medal almost feeling like the

1028
01:38:17,067 --> 01:38:24,457
Yes, well I think the weight of expectation was well and truly on his shoulders and he and he simply didn't dive quite as well as he did in the semis.

1029
01:38:27,521 --> 01:38:29,524
It's about delivering when the medals are on offer.

1030
01:38:29,543 --> 01:38:37,135
Those earlier scores of course don't carry forward to the final and Padaya saves his best when it matters.

1031
01:38:39,158 --> 01:38:42,282
Bronze and silver his haul from these

1032
01:38:44,167 --> 01:38:45,470
Olympic Games.

1033
01:38:45,570 --> 01:38:53,246
The World Championships are in Barcelona for swimming next year when these divers will recongregate.

1034
01:38:54,427 --> 01:39:03,265
They will have to be right at their very best to match a show like this but it's that Olympic title that is the big one.

1035
01:39:03,326 --> 01:39:05,350
That's what makes you a diving

1036
01:39:06,780 --> 01:39:14,229
So we won't be far away from a medal presentation, and nearly everyone is staying for it.

1037
01:39:14,248 --> 01:39:14,869
And so are we.

1038
01:39:16,372 --> 01:39:18,493
I've been impressed with the way crowds have stayed.

1039
01:39:19,095 --> 01:39:28,045
You know, the extra minutes to, even if there's been no British competitor on the day, I did a lot of sessions of gymnastics and observed that that was the case every time.

1040
01:39:28,945 --> 01:39:31,488
And that makes a difference to the athletes, Roger.

1041
01:39:31,469 --> 01:39:54,033
well the pool it has to be said was hopelessly one-sided in its support but within that there was still a full emotional range throughout the three sessions of the diving for those divers who really performed brilliantly and those who may be disappointed one's got to say that those slightly disappointing marks for the top guys in the last round or two were

1042
01:39:54,014 --> 01:40:05,131
Fairly enthusiastically received by the crowd but in general the atmosphere has been very special and it's another successful competition in these London 2012 games.

1043
01:40:06,873 --> 01:40:12,203
Walking to the Aquatic Centre across the Olympic Park past the stadium this evening.

1044
01:40:12,443 --> 01:40:20,055
The atmosphere around it was a glorious summer's evening and you can't always say that in Stratford even in August and the atmosphere was great.

1045
01:40:20,034 --> 01:40:21,917
every different country was mixing.

1046
01:40:21,936 --> 01:40:24,520
There were loads of Dutch fans going to see the hockey.

1047
01:40:25,161 --> 01:40:44,101
Everybody's streaming there with their colors and the atmosphere was absolutely special as it has been throughout two weeks and for everybody lucky enough to get a ticket in here tonight then this competition and the drama and the excitement of it all and a happy enough ending for the crowd has really topped it off.

1048
01:40:44,082 --> 01:40:45,203
It's been special.

1049
01:40:45,583 --> 01:41:08,554
Yeah and when you enjoy an evening like tonight outside especially as you say Roger you realize you just blow away all your cynicism about the Olympics whatever that those cynicisms might be and rejoice in the human spirit that's and the goodness that's out there and the happiness that it generates on a night like tonight when it's just a great fun to be around Olympic Park.

1050
01:41:08,533 --> 01:41:10,277
This is what it's all about.

1051
01:41:10,877 --> 01:41:15,926
When you bring an Olympics to a city, you hope to capture that and it's been done here, that's for sure.

1052
01:41:16,606 --> 01:41:21,836
And a big contributor to that every time when it works is the volunteers.

1053
01:41:21,895 --> 01:41:24,399
The quality and the attitude of the volunteers.

1054
01:41:24,500 --> 01:41:25,983
I've been really impressed.

1055
01:41:26,042 --> 01:41:34,676
I've been lucky enough to attend six Olympics and no one's done it better than here in terms of making everyone from overseas and locally feel so welcome.

1056
01:41:35,887 --> 01:41:36,988
Well, that's terrific to hear.

1057
01:41:37,029 --> 01:41:40,813
I've been around quite a few different events during the last two weeks.

1058
01:41:40,853 --> 01:42:01,895
Not all have been gold medal events, but weightlifting and rowing, a real range of sports, handball even, and the arena's been packed out and you get supporters turning up watching sports they know nothing about and people they know nothing about and paying quite a bit of money for it and just being delighted to be there and be a part of it.

1059
01:42:01,876 --> 01:42:06,203
If you're just joining us we're awaiting the medal presentation for the 10 meter platform.

1060
01:42:06,805 --> 01:42:10,251
A quite sensational evening of competition.

1061
01:42:15,479 --> 01:42:26,078
Tinged with a little bit of drama and sadness for the injury to Martin Wolfram with the what we suspect was a shoulder dislocation on his last dive.

1062
01:42:27,880 --> 01:42:52,470
the word about the Chinese divers as well because the standards they've set and the way that they have hauled the sport forwards with their exemplary performances in no way is it decrying their efforts because people are almost celebrating that they've been beaten it's a it is a backhanded compliment here in that way that they've set their standards so high but it does prove that nobody wins all the time every time

1063
01:42:52,449 --> 01:43:10,931
And what it proves too is that in the last round pressure puts a microscope on your ability to cope with what's happening and sometimes you can just expose a weakness that maybe you can deal with in years to come once you've had the experience of dealing with it.

1064
01:43:11,283 --> 01:43:30,733
I think that's what David Badaar in particular did because he was following Tom Daley, the crowd were really up, the Chinese were next and he always seemed to respond and kept that pressure on the two Chinese divers and to some extent, to two different extents, they did crack.

1065
01:43:30,752 --> 01:43:36,902
Now we're ready for that victory ceremony which will be raucously supported

1066
01:43:37,912 --> 01:43:38,932
from all quarters.

1067
01:43:39,253 --> 01:43:41,818
They are really going to enjoy the next 10 minutes.

1068
01:43:52,592 --> 01:43:56,779
We've got two very happy men and a slightly disconsolate Choubo.

1069
01:43:57,840 --> 01:43:59,502
He really expected to win.

1070
01:43:59,561 --> 01:44:06,332
His country expected him to, but any competitor should be proud and pleased to receive silver.

1071
01:44:09,451 --> 01:44:17,264
You're feeling that in golden bronze, they're really going to enjoy this.

1072
01:44:27,983 --> 01:44:33,972
And he was vice president of the Beijing Games organizing committee for six years.

1073
01:44:35,556 --> 01:44:39,541
He might just have been expecting to present a gold medal to one of his countrymen.

1074
01:44:45,768 --> 01:44:53,695
President of FINA, Dr. Julio Cesar Malione, who is from Uruguay, presents the flowers.

1075
01:44:56,798 --> 01:44:59,742
Tom Bailey can't get up on that platform quick enough.

1076
01:45:03,130 --> 01:45:08,555
The first 10-meter medal for Great Britain since 1960.

1077
01:45:08,576 --> 01:45:09,938
52 years.

1078
01:45:10,318 --> 01:45:11,099
Just listen to this.

1079
01:45:20,649 --> 01:45:24,154
Every mum throughout the land would be saying, ah, bless him, won't they?

1080
01:45:24,755 --> 01:45:30,521
Yeah, that's a smile that you'll see across newspapers across the world.

1081
01:45:34,297 --> 01:45:44,813
He's got to be a hard man not to really have your heart go out to him what he's been through and he'll be thinking of his late father in this moment, I'm absolutely sure.

1082
01:45:49,220 --> 01:45:51,363
He's got to be one of the happiest bronze medals of the games.

1083
01:45:51,622 --> 01:45:57,792
I think so, and you can see the gesture to the crowd that is saying, yes, thank you for your support, this is for you too.

1084
01:46:00,150 --> 01:46:07,899
For Chubo, more dazzling skills, but just for once, the world champion has to miss out.

1085
01:46:16,087 --> 01:46:18,989
Well, that's the unpredictability of sport.

1086
01:46:19,010 --> 01:46:20,570
The hottest of favorites coming in.

1087
01:46:22,632 --> 01:46:28,639
But he didn't reckon, perhaps, on the performance of David Budaya.

1088
01:46:31,622 --> 01:46:36,087
He chose his moment to produce an outstanding evening's competition.

1089
01:46:36,908 --> 01:46:43,956
And a bit of a smile at last from the 19 year old and the gracious bow from all the Chinese divers as ever.

1090
01:46:45,238 --> 01:46:49,301
But it takes a great diver to win a great competition.

1091
01:46:50,524 --> 01:46:52,786
And the gold medalist is from the United States.

1092
01:46:52,985 --> 01:46:57,430
The good days are rolling again for diving in the States.

1093
01:46:57,490 --> 01:46:59,233
David Budai wins the gold.

1094
01:47:07,177 --> 01:47:33,877
to think that less than two tenths of a point separated the top three divers coming into that last round he held his nerve he pulled out a 102.6 to win it and to win it by a couple of points well done David and his experience having been to a games before maybe that helped him and we'll say it one final time he nearly didn't even make the semi-final

1095
01:47:43,172 --> 01:47:56,439
The United States of America.

1096
01:48:28,010 --> 01:48:31,354
I'm sorry.

1097
01:48:57,945 --> 01:49:05,492
You can hardly believe it.

1098
01:49:07,699 --> 01:49:13,228
I just want to shoot you the ranking of where he was after each series of dives.

1099
01:49:13,429 --> 01:49:18,536
Equal first after the first, equal third, first, first, equal second, and first.

1100
01:49:18,817 --> 01:49:20,979
He was the most consistent man.

1101
01:49:21,421 --> 01:49:23,904
We talked about quality and consistency at the start.

1102
01:49:24,225 --> 01:49:29,131
David Badaia delivered it, and he's been delivered a gold medal.

1103
01:49:30,774 --> 01:49:31,496
Nobody's going.

1104
01:49:31,695 --> 01:49:33,679
Nobody's gone for the early bus, have they?

1105
01:49:33,698 --> 01:49:34,180
No.

1106
01:49:37,787 --> 01:49:41,211
And Chubo was only in front after the second series of dives.

1107
01:49:41,811 --> 01:49:46,617
Equal fourth after the first, then first, second, second, second, second.

1108
01:49:47,037 --> 01:49:48,018
Never quite cracked it.

1109
01:49:50,560 --> 01:49:54,824
Well, they will pose for the photographs now and enjoy the moment.

1110
01:49:55,164 --> 01:49:59,609
I think Tom Daley is going to do his own victory lap in front of all these supporters.

1111
01:49:59,789 --> 01:50:05,735
Now they can take the photographs and use their flash guns as much as they want.

1112
01:50:07,132 --> 01:50:09,016
Now he's going up into the crowd there.

1113
01:50:15,912 --> 01:50:17,515
He's going to make the most of this moment.

1114
01:50:19,801 --> 01:50:21,003
He's trying to steal the show.

1115
01:50:21,043 --> 01:50:23,048
David Budayev doesn't mind.

1116
01:50:23,470 --> 01:50:24,551
He's got the gold.

1117
01:50:25,695 --> 01:50:31,502
They're really supposed to march around together so that the photographers can get the shot of the three of them together.

1118
01:50:31,563 --> 01:50:36,028
But David Budaya has been thrown the stars and stripes.

1119
01:50:37,390 --> 01:50:38,069
That's all good.

1120
01:50:39,692 --> 01:50:41,975
We're nearly at the end of the journey, aren't we, Roger?

1121
01:50:42,015 --> 01:50:48,682
And there's a sense of almost melancholy and sadness that this great party is coming to an end.

1122
01:50:50,564 --> 01:50:52,226
They're going to celebrate as well.

1123
01:50:56,475 --> 01:50:59,664
There is a great camaraderie, one senses, between the divers.

1124
01:51:06,784 --> 01:51:07,407
Great stuff.

1125
01:51:07,426 --> 01:51:09,011
Just enjoy these scenes there.

1126
01:51:10,113 --> 01:51:11,176
Moments to cherish.

1127
01:51:19,831 --> 01:51:44,067
I hope Chubo also realizes the part he played and what a contribution he's made to 10 meter platform diving and just throw in here too Roger that you don't get a wonderful competition like this unless you've got three or four guys competing at the very top providing you with real drama it's not really as exciting if one man races away with it

1128
01:51:44,046 --> 01:51:49,913
to have Chubo and Tom Daly there pushing Budair all the way and to get the surprise result.

1129
01:51:50,755 --> 01:51:52,957
This is one of the great competitions you'll see in diving.

1130
01:51:56,122 --> 01:51:58,984
You need more than one man to be standing up and giving you a story.

1131
01:52:01,667 --> 01:52:05,632
So a great competition for the United States.

1132
01:52:06,118 --> 01:52:14,628
who got off to a good start with David Budaya winning bronze in that 10 meter synchro and it gave the rest of the American diving team a bit of momentum.

1133
01:52:15,090 --> 01:52:16,832
He started it and boy has he finished it.

1134
01:52:23,079 --> 01:52:26,524
Six out of eight then for Chinese diving.

1135
01:52:28,850 --> 01:52:44,073
three meters and ten meters for men let it down and when you set your standard so high you can understand disappointment with silver but Tom Daly pretty happy with bronze to say the least

1136
01:52:46,095 --> 01:52:53,006
Well, the blow torch of Olympic competition shows the strengths and frailties of the athlete.

1137
01:52:54,349 --> 01:53:00,078
We saw all of that tonight and we've come away with a wonderful feeling about the health of the sport.

1138
01:53:01,320 --> 01:53:07,210
The competitors who give us the pleasure from it and just delighted to have been here.

1139
01:53:07,847 --> 01:53:21,972
United States got a silver in the women's three-meter synchro and a couple of bronze in the men's three-meter synchro as well with Ipsen, Jumei, and Johnston and Bryant getting that women's silver.

1140
01:53:22,033 --> 01:53:26,480
So, a gold, a silver and two bronze for the United States.

1141
01:53:27,439 --> 01:53:29,722
Well, this party's going to carry on for quite some time.

1142
01:53:29,963 --> 01:53:38,395
Steve, thank you very much for your contribution as we confirm the final result and some dazzling statistical work, if I might say so.

1143
01:53:38,676 --> 01:53:41,801
For an artistic sport, you can certainly crunch a few numbers.

1144
01:53:42,502 --> 01:53:44,685
Well, the statistics are also important, aren't they?

1145
01:53:44,786 --> 01:53:53,599
When you're looking at degrees of difficulty and execution, the number that really matters is the man who's on top at the end, and David Badiah.

1146
01:53:53,578 --> 01:54:03,435
particularly with that 102 last dive to produce that under pressure, reminiscent in some ways of the finish in Beijing four years ago.

1147
01:54:03,475 --> 01:54:11,426
Remember some of those names down the bottom end, just teenagers in their first Olympic Games.

1148
01:54:11,507 --> 01:54:16,194
They will be competing, but the standard is set so high.

1149
01:54:18,114 --> 01:54:26,634
Now the end of a couple of astonishing weeks of great competition in this aquatic center.

1150
01:54:28,597 --> 01:54:33,047
Seventeen thousand capacity and boy have they all had their moneys worth.

1151
01:54:33,068 --> 01:54:36,494
A great competition here in the ten meter platform diving.

1152
01:54:38,466 --> 01:54:47,340
And I think there's a bit of a party going to be happening in the United States camp and also in the British camp.

1153
01:54:47,359 --> 01:54:57,774
If you're scared of heights, look away now as we take you to the edge of the platform and consider what the competitors had six times over.

1154
01:54:59,222 --> 01:55:01,945
And before you worry, that is an automatic suspended camera.

1155
01:55:01,966 --> 01:55:04,128
There's not some poor chap holding that one.

1156
01:55:04,829 --> 01:55:14,360
But again, just to recap here, it was an American gold, a Chinese silver, and a very British bronze here in the 10 meter platform.

1157
01:55:15,021 --> 01:55:19,306
Leave you just to enjoy these final few memories from this great night of competition.

1158
01:55:19,327 --> 01:55:21,670
We certainly hope you've enjoyed it.

1159
01:55:31,505 --> 01:55:40,844
Hard to remember it all, but I'm sure you'll remember some of it and especially the end and the joy of victory for Badiah and bronze for Daley.

1160
01:55:41,164 --> 01:55:47,757
A great night off the platform and it was again just our pleasure to bring it to you.

1161
01:56:57,516 --> 01:56:59,189
you

